Here's a cheat I discovered that I've never heard anyone make a comment on.
But man is it worse than the save and restore method!

This cheat requires you to have some stuff you want to have multiple copies of.
or want to give to another character without haveing a bones file.

While playing a game you drop all the goodes you want of next to a staircase.
The location doesn't matter but it's convient to be next to a stair case.

Take the stairs to the other level then hit the escape key to exit out to the
operation system.  I'm on a PC machine but I know it works for Unix machines too
if you have access to the game levels.  Change directories to where the current
levels are being run.  Copy the level with the goodies on it to a temp file
Type exit returning you to your game.  Return to the level you came from and
pick up your goodies.  Take the stairs again.  Exit to the OS and copy the temp
file back over the level you took the goodies from.

Go back to the game and pick up you goodies again.  You now have twice as many.

Repeat the whole process if you want to double again or just repeat 
the last copy if you only the same abount again.

Warning don't copy the temp file to the wrong level.  You'll die by a trickery!

If you ever get a good character have him run back to the 1st level.  Have
him drop his goodies and save the level for other games just starting!
Real easy way to get all your equipment for a first level character.

Another warning Raise level potions are not good things to duplicate for
beginning characters.  Hard monsters come real fast and you die sooner.
Work you way up throught the levels with your toys.

Has anyone else found this?
